<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!-- ========================================================================
       TWILEK_TROPE_GENES_MOVE_1, wave 2.

       Wave 1 (fc16d5507, 2026-09-17) removed Turn_Gene_AgressionSubmissive,
       Libido_High and Beauty_Beautiful from RSW_RimMandrakeTwilek's endogene
       list; the slavery-trope stereotype is no longer a species-wide
       guarantee. This file is the other half: making each trope a fact that
       can be true of any INDIVIDUAL pawn, any race, rather than a fact about
       a race.

       Route taken, and why: vanilla's normal trait-generation system already
       rolls TraitDefs onto every humanlike pawn independent of xenotype;
       no Harmony hook needed, unlike forcing a GENE onto an arbitrary pawn
       (which the wave-1 note correctly identified as needing a real Harmony
       postfix against the Biotech gene API; that stays owed, see below).

       Per-gene disposition, checked against the real GeneDef/TraitDef XML via
       RimSage before writing anything here (2026-09-24):

       * Beauty_Beautiful: NOTHING BUILT. Vanilla Core already ships a
         "Beauty" TraitDef whose degree 2 ("beautiful") carries the identical
         <statOffsets><PawnBeauty>2</PawnBeauty></statOffsets> the gene gave,
         rolled individually for any pawn of any race by the ordinary trait
         generator. The architecture goal is already satisfied for this one;
         building a second beauty mechanism would just be a duplicate.

       * Turn_Gene_AgressionSubmissive: RM_Submissive below. The donor gene
         (Integrated Genes, turnovus.biotech.integratedgenes) carries exactly
         two behavioural stat effects: socialFightChanceFactor 0.25 and a
         SlaveSuppressionFallRate factor of 0.5 (both confirmed live fields on
         the real GeneDef via RimSage). TraitDegreeData supports the same two
         fields directly, so this is a faithful, not approximate, port;
         just individually rolled instead of racially guaranteed.

       * Libido_High: RM_Amorous below. The donor gene's only field is
         lovinMTBFactor 0.5 (RimSage-confirmed), which JobDriver_Lovin reads
         off Pawn.genes and off any Hediff carrying
         HediffComp_GiveLovinMTBFactor, CONFIRMED (Source/RimWorld/
         JobDriver_Lovin.cs, GenerateRandomMinTicksToNextLovin). TraitDegreeData
         (Source/RimWorld/TraitDegreeData.cs) has no field that reaches either
         path, and BackstoryDef (Source/RimWorld/BackstoryDef.cs) can only
         force other TRAITS, never a gene or a hediff; so a trait cannot
         replicate the lovin'-frequency multiplier itself without a Harmony
         postfix on GenerateRandomMinTicksToNextLovin or on trait-add. That
         narrow piece is OWED, same as wave 1 already flagged for the gene
         route, now scoped to exactly this one mechanic, not to all three
         genes. RM_Amorous instead uses a real, verifiable field
         (disallowedThoughts) to give a forward, thick-skinned-about-rejection
         personality a genuine in-game consequence without guessing at an
         unreachable stat.

       Both TraitDefs are RM_-tier (NAMING_SCHEME_PLAN.md): nothing about a
       "submissive" or "amorous" personality is Star-Wars-specific, and tier
       is about what the CONTENT is, not which mod folder ships it first.
  ======================================================================== -->

  <TraitDef>
    <defName>RM_Submissive</defName>
    <commonality>3</commonality>
    <conflictingTraits>
      <li>Bloodlust</li>
    </conflictingTraits>
    <degreeDatas>
      <li>
        <label>submissive</label>
        <description>{PAWN_nameDef} finds a real sense of comfort in following someone else's lead, and rarely picks a fight. If {PAWN_pronoun} ever ends up enslaved, {PAWN_pronoun} settles into it more easily than most.</description>
        <degree>0</degree>
        <socialFightChanceFactor>0.25</socialFightChanceFactor>
        <statFactors>
          <SlaveSuppressionFallRate>0.5</SlaveSuppressionFallRate>
        </statFactors>
      </li>
    </degreeDatas>
  </TraitDef>

  <TraitDef>
    <defName>RM_Amorous</defName>
    <commonality>3</commonality>
    <degreeDatas>
      <li>
        <label>amorous</label>
        <description>{PAWN_nameDef} pursues romance eagerly and openly, and a rebuff barely slows {PAWN_objective} down.</description>
        <degree>0</degree>
        <disallowedThoughts>
          <li>RebuffedMyRomanceAttempt</li>
          <li>FailedRomanceAttemptOnMe</li>
          <li>FailedRomanceAttemptOnMeLowOpinionMood</li>
        </disallowedThoughts>
      </li>
    </degreeDatas>
  </TraitDef>

</Defs>
